## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
TER is a fab-lite company, making it dependent on foundries, which exposes it to semiconductor capex cycles. The company’s revenue concentration in data center customers (vs. consumer markets) provides some stability but also ties its performance to hyperscale trends. Inventory digestion and CapEx positioning remain key risks, as the semiconductor industry faces a weak macroeconomic backdrop.  

